Keeps an input method's composition in the field composing it on Linux when another client's input
type changes (#3154). InputMethodAuraLinux::OnTextInputTypeChanged refocused its context for any
client that called it, focused or not, where InputMethodBase and the Windows input methods ignore
one that isn't focused. Under Wayland refocusing disables and enables text-input-v3, and the
compositor deactivates and activates the input method, which drops its preedit. So when ilo's
command bar took the keys and the page's field blurred, a composition typed into the bar while
the page's keys were held was left drawn in the bar but no longer the input method's to finish.

--- a/ui/base/ime/linux/input_method_auralinux.cc
+++ b/ui/base/ime/linux/input_method_auralinux.cc
@@ -380,6 +380,12 @@
 }
 
 void InputMethodAuraLinux::OnTextInputTypeChanged(TextInputClient* client) {
+  // browser_core: a client that isn't the focused one, as a page whose field blurs while ilo's
+  // own field has the input method, changes nothing here, as in InputMethodBase; refocusing the
+  // context would reset the input method under the focused client's composition (#3154).
+  if (!IsTextInputClientFocused(client)) {
+    return;
+  }
   UpdateContextFocusState();
   InputMethodBase::OnTextInputTypeChanged(client);
   // TODO(yoichio): Support inputmode HTML attribute.
